WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:29.960
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.830
It's really hot today.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.290
Yeah.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:46.460
I want some cold juice to drink.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.670
You're really relaxed.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.540
T-Taiga!

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.750
T-Taiga!

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:57.220
Are you guys taking a rest, knowing that our next opponent is the strong Teijin High School?

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.680
Um... That is...

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:03.470
In the first game, you three combined went 2-for-13.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.810
You must have gone easy on them.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.980
That was nice of you, Senpai.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.270
W-Well, let's continue practicing our batting!

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.820
M-Me too.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.360
Let's beat Teijin.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.530
Geez.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:25.910
Hattori.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.620
Could you catch a bit for me?

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.210
I might be pitching in the next game.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.130
Yeah.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.220
Nice ball!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.510
Shimizu-kun.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.730
It's about the freshmen that went out running.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.350
It's been 40 minutes now, and they still haven't returned.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.190
Don't you think they're a bit late?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.690
Here it comes!

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.320
Shibuya!

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.240
Take it easy!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.580
I didn't bring my helmet!

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.160
You're a wimp.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.660
H-Hey...

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.080
Shouldn't we be heading back?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.250
They must be waiting for us.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.920
Don't care. Don't care.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.970
They probably won't let us do any decent training anyway.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.340
That isn't baseball.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:23.930
H-Hey...

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.930
H-Hey...

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.770
What are you doing?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.440
Captain...

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:39.400
Didn't I tell you all to practice fielding after running?

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.320
But training is boring.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:48.740
We've only been training dull stuff like fitness, bunting, and practicing our connection plays.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:53.080
Say that when you can bunt properly.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.710
There's no need to bunt.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:04:01.220
I'll hold them back in the second game with my 150 km/h fastballs again!

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.970
Isn't 145 km/h enough?

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.260
I'll hit 150 km/h in the next game!

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.390
I'll hold back Teijin's offense with zero runs,
and I'll hit homeruns when I bat.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.890
I'll win the next game single-handedly.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.600
H-Hey, that's impossible.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.730
You idiot!

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.820
The basics of baseball are homeruns and strikeouts!

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.490
<i>Simple minded... overconfident... and a braggart.</i>

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.700
<i>Simple minded... overconfident... and a braggart.</i>

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.200
<i>Simple minded... overconfident... and a braggart.</i>

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.450
<i>He's really... annoying!</i>

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.910
<i>He's really... annoying!</i>

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.830
In the first game, we got a shutout.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.380
We may even go to Koshien-

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.380
All right. All right.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.960
Let's leave this idiot and go back.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.090
Yes.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:42.800
Shigeno-senpai must have said the same thing.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:49.890
I joined the Seishuu baseball club because I adored Shigeno-senpai.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.270
I refused all the other offers into strong schools,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.230
and chose Seishuu because I saw Shigeno-senpai pitch against Kaido last year,

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:01.610
throwing until he collapsed.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:07.160
These guys here achieved a lot during their senior year in junior high,

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:12.450
but they all came here, to Seishuu's baseball club, because they all admired Shigeno-senpai's heroic baseball!

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.540
But since we joined, all we've been doing is basic training techniques.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.170
To be honest, I feel let down.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.420
You shouldn't say it that way...

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.050
Stop it, Shibuya!

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.550
You should just tell them outright!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.840
You guys have been complaining that training is boring too.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:33.850
Really?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:34.930
W-Well...

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:35.640
W-Well...

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.980
Yes.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:40.900
We would like to do more actual game training, maybe...

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:43.780
I see.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.360
I understand.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.410
Why don't you all practice your batting,
or whatever you want as much as you like then?

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:51.490
We'll have open training until the game the day after tomorrow.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.000
Could you pass that on to the seniors too?

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:55.700
See you.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:56.870
Wait!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.250
This baseball club was originally made by Shigeno-senpai,

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.090
and it's not like I became captain because I wanted to.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.010
Shimizu-kun.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.060
Shimizu-kun...

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.270
I'm back.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.270
Huh?

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:18.850
You're early, Taiga.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.770
Isn't your next game the day after tomorrow?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.070
Who knows?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.730
"Who knows?" What's that supposed to mean!?

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.490
You're the captain!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.570
Am I?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.670
<i>It seems the baseball club got some new members.</i>

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.800
<i>Oh yeah?</i>

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.050
<i>Then maybe they'll get far this time?</i>

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.380
<i>Impossible. Impossible.</i>

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:52.390
<i>They don't have Shigeno-senpai this year.</i>

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.720
<i>Oh yeah.</i>

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.310
<i>Hey,</i>

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.650
<i>didn't Shigeno-senpai join the Memphis Bats?</i>

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.980
<i>Yeah, that's what Yamada-sensei was saying.</i>

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.820
<i>Look at this.</i>

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.910
<i>Saves?</i>

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.080
<i>So he's not even a starter.</i>

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:20.250
<i>Three weeks after the beginning of the season, the Bats are in last place in the Eastern Division.</i>

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:24.210
<i>So even Shigeno-senpai can't make a difference.</i>

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.880
<i>Even if you lose in the first game,</i>

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.420
<i>you guys should just make your own team.</i>

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:34.390
<i>Just take it easy, new captain.</i>

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.810
<i>Don't talk like a big shot.</i>

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:40.310
<i>You couldn't achieve anything either.</i>

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.440
Shimizu-kun.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:49.610
Wait!

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.400
Are you really going home?

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.360
The game is tomorrow!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.700
I said we're going to have open training.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.450
But what about teamwork?

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.410
We all have to work together today-

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:05.460
Shibuya-kun said he's going to win it single-handedly,

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.590
so why don't we let him win for us?

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:08.590
Shimizu-kun!

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.720
Oh? You're all having an open training session before the game?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.930
Shimizu-kun sure made a ballsy decision.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:25.940
Sensei, this is not the time to be admiring him!

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.440
He's just being stubborn!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.820
I see there is no end to your worries as the manager.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.870
It seems Shimizu-kun and Shibuya-kun are clashing a lot, aren't they?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.490
Yes...

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:44.420
Shimizu-kun said that Shibuya-kun is like Shigeno-senpai and that annoys him.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.960
Shibuya-kun and Nogoro-kun?

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.210
I see.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.260
I don't think so.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.010
Huh?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:56.510
One of the good things about youth is that you can fight each others' opinions.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.970
Well, let's just believe in their teamwork.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.230
Nice ball, Shibuya!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.440
Hey,

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.860
do you think it's all right for us to be practicing as we like?

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.570
I guess so.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:19.200
Shibuya seems to be in good form,
so we should be fine leaving it all to him.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.620
Hey!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.330
You're the new members of the Seishuu baseball club, right?

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.500
You must be...

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.920
Tashiro-senpai!

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.960
Oh, so you've heard of me.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.590
Of course.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:37.340
You're Seishuu's former clean-up hitter.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.850
Are you now on a university baseball team?

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.350
I'm a rounin.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.510
Don't make me say it again.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.020
Your second game is tomorrow, right?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.610
Why are you practicing here?

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.860
Where are Taiga and the rest-

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.860
Tashiro-senpai!

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.360
I'm Shibuya.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:54.780
I'm the starting pitcher.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.740
Oh, so you're the freshman ace everyone's been talking about.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.660
I hear you throw well.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:02.080
Senpai.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.290
If you're free, could you please catch my pitching?

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:07.670
Y-You idiot!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.000
That's rude!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.500
All right.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.340
Throw it.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:21.100
All right! Come!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.270
Nice pitch!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.190
I see why you were able to shutout the other team in the first game.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.360
Who do you think is better? Shigeno-senpai or me? {M: I split the line}

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:37.610
What?

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:41.530
I plan on exceeding Shigeno-senpai.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:45.580
I'll completely shutout all of Kaido's batters with this pitch.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.400
Kaido?

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.250
You still have the game against Teijin tomorrow!

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.460
I don't see them as a threat.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.800
I also said that to Captain Shimizu.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:00.720
I told him I'll pitch, hit, and win the second game single-handedly.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.890
Don't joke around!

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:06.270
The summer tournament finishes if you lose just one game!

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:11.600
Each team will come against you desperately, carrying their pride!

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.730
You're going to win by yourself!?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.280
Don't take baseball lightly!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:23.910
This is a free fansub.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:23.910
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.700
Are you ready?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.410
Yeah. Come!

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.000
Here it comes!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.840
That was a weak dive.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.380
Hit better grounders then!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.630
These are within the infield, right?

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.550
I'm in the outfield.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.050
All right! Come!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.140
Everyone!

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:48.270
Let's go to Shibuya-kun and the rest of the team now.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:52.900
It's not right for the team to be practicing apart.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:57.400
But this open practice was Captain Taiga's decision, right?

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:00.320
But this is just irresponsible!

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:04.110
Please tell Shimizu-kun that as his senpai!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.910
We can't...

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:13.250
The reason why Taiga makes us practice the basic plays is for our own good.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.130
At our skill level,

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.300
we can't play strongly like Shigeno-senpai,

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:22.800
but we can keep a game going if we can execute continuous basic plays.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.720
We had a lot of new recruits with baseball experience this year,

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:30.850
so we thought we'd be on the bench, but...

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:33.060
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.980
<i>They may have had some experience during their senior years,</i>

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.730
<i>but it's no match to yours, who pushed Kaido to their limit.{fought against Kaido for full innings.}</i>

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.400
<i>B-But still...</i>

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.700
<i>B-But still...</i>

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:47.660
<i>It was all of you who made the Seishuu baseball club when we still didn't have a field.</i>

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.700
<i>Please have more confidence in yourselves.</i>

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.870
So we'd like to be able to do this at least,

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.040
and not let Taiga down.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.750
And we started in our sophomore year,

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.010
so this is our last summer.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.380
Senpai...

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.140
U-Um...

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.430
We're sorry for practicing as we please!

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:13.600
Our ideas were naive...

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.480
and we now think...

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:19.190
it's important to practice the basic skills too.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:22.530
Please let us practice with you, Senpai!

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.990
Please!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.700
Please!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:29.280
Yeah, let's all practice together!

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.540
Now we can practice catching proper grounders.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.660
Everyone get in your fielding positions!

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:36.870
Yes!

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.400
Here.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.650
This is the scoresheet from Teijin High School's first game.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.570
Make sure you look through it.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.320
Is that all?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:12.240
Didn't you come here to complain to me?

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:19.210
Well, all the senpai and Yamada-sensei believe in you, Shimizu-kun.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.590
It would be stupid if I was the only one getting all worked up about it, wouldn't it?

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:27.420
So I decided to believe in you too, Shimizu-kun.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.010
Let's do our best tomorrow!

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:39.020
Taiga!

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.150
Have you got a moment?

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.190
Why don't you check on your computer?

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.410
It's not running too well.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:52.200
Aren't you curious about Honda's record too?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.910
Not really...

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:57.290
Here it is!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.160
And the Memphis Bats?

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.960
51 wins and 38 losses.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:05.300
They're at the top of the Eastern Division, six games ahead of second place.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.430
When I checked last week, it was only four games.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.680
So they pushed them further down.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.260
They've got to win now!

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.180
<i>In April, they were in last place.</i>

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:19.560
And how about the individual records?

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:21.690
Hey.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:24.400
He's at the top of the league with 25 saves.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.780
He's working hard.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.030
<i>He's going to affect the others.</i>

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:38.660
<i>His fighting spirit is going to affect the people around him to the point that it's unbelievable. {M: from S3 ep 10}</i>

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:42.460
<i>Just take it easy, new captain.</i>

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:48.670
<i>He's annoying, even when he's in America.</i>

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:57.180
Just you watch!

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.600
I'm going to win it with a complete game shutout!

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:12.530
All right!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:13.570
Let's go!

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:14.870
Yeah!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.910
Seishuu, huh?

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:24.080
They don't have that monster pitcher this year, so let's return the favor.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.880
Batting first, shortstop: Shimizu-kun.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:29.710
Play ball!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:33.220
Strike!

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:34.840
It's fast...

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.890
As expected from a renowned school.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.970
It's different from the first game.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.320
All right!

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:51.360
All right! He did it!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.280
Batting second, second baseman: Hattori-kun.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.280
Go Hattori!

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:11.130
Out!

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:19.640
Out!

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.560
All right!

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:24.770
First run!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.690
Batting fourth, pitcher: Shibuya-kun.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.740
<i>We don't need basic strategies.</i>

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:37.570
<i>I'll crush them with one swing!</i>

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.330
Out!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.760
<i>Well, one run is enough.</i>

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.010
Strike!

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.520
Strike!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.980
Batter out!

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.330
Ball!

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.380
Ball four!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.050
How many has Shibuya-kun thrown now?

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.050
70 with the next pitch.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.560
<i>A complete game shutout? This is pathetic.</i>

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:48.190
<i>So this is my strength at the end.</i>

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:52.610
<i>I wish they'd hurry up and sub me...</i>

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.240
<i>Oh, I see...</i>

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:00.450
<i>He's not annoying me because he's like Shigeno-senpai.</i>

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:07.160
<i>It's because he says big things, but he's weak and can't deal with a setback.</i>

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:12.840
<i>He's like I was back then.</i>

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:21.970
Foul!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.180
Shibuya!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:27.350
The batter swings slowly!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:28.730
Your pitches are fast!

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:29.940
Be more confident!

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.600
This is just your 50th pitch!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.570
It's too early to be giving up!

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:36.150
50th pitch?

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.900
<i>Taiga!</i>

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.530
<i>You haven't even pitched 50 pitches. It's too early to get tired.</i>

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.030
<i>Put all you've got into it!</i>

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.000
<i>Shimizu-kun...</i>

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.540
Strike!

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:54.420
What?

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.920
The power in his pitches has returned.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:19:59.170
Strike!

00:19:59.170 --> 00:19:59.970
Batter out!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:00.720
All right!

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:01.680
Two outs!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:03.390
Nice pitching, Shibuya!

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:13.770
Out!

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:15.560
Wow! Wow!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:17.360
They got through without giving up any runs!

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:40.210
Well, they hung in there and did a good job of loading the bases after getting two outs.

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.010
Yes.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.180
<i>Everyone, do your best.</i>

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.050
Captain.

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:50.140
I can still throw five more innings,

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:52.310
so it's okay if it's a draw.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.520
Oh really?

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:01.820
<i>Idiot.</i>

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.610
<i>You don't even have the strength left to stand.</i>

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.170
Safe!

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:18.590
Nice, Shimizu-kun!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:19.630
Captain! {M: Can't make out all of it}

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:36.980
Strike!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:37.980
Batter out!

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:39.270
Game over!

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:40.860
We did it!

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:48.870
Starting tomorrow, we'll be going back to our regular practice.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.040
And we'll be increasing it by 50%.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:52.660
5-50%...

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:53.910
5-50%...

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:55.370
S-Seriously?

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.580
It might have been better if we had just lost the game and retired.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:01.130
Well, good job today!

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:03.340
Good job!

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:08.220
<i>Shimizu-kun now has the face of a captain.</i>

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:08.930
All right!

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:11.850
I'll finish the third game with a complete game shutout!

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:12.890
Again?

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.180
You sure talk big after giving up six runs.

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:17.440
Shut up!

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:18.520
Manager.

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:22.610
In tomorrow's game, our opponent for the third game will be decided, so...

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:23.940
Sure!

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:26.070
I'll go check them out.

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:30.490
Why don't we go together?

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:36.910
Okay!

00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:11.550
What?

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:13.970
Shimizu's going on a group blind date?

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:15.220
I see.

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:17.350
She must be enjoying her campus life.

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:22.350
Well, I think I'll go watch a Major League game for a change!

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:23.520
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:25.190
A Thing to Aim For.

00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:27.820
Run to the stage of your dreams!
